## 021ea70e8ed8

**Reproduced teaching ambiguity** for generator SHA-256 `308b4a6694158373974f7c170ace1953e39eaef79c87358687b26a2a60cc7053`; executed canonical rule hash `abdf780ecbe7`.

Plausible rival:

> In any column with at least two nonzero cells all of the same color, fill from the first occupied row through the last, even if the column contains a third same-color endpoint.

This rival fits the canonical examples because their connecting columns contain exactly two matching endpoints. It also fits all three generated demonstrations from `seed=0`, `difficulty=None`, sample indexes **9, 10, 11**. The generated query at sample index **12** contains a three-cell color-1 column at rows 0, 3, and 6. The intended rule leaves that column unchanged because it has three occupied cells; the rival fills rows 0–6 with color 1. A separate valid two-endpoint color-2 column still connects under both rules.

All four inputs pass the target's current `self_check`. Canonical Racket outputs match the recorded intended outputs for 4/4 grids; the rival fits 3/3 demonstrations and differs on the query. Exact artifacts:

- generated lesson, intended outputs, rival outputs, source recipe: `checks/audit/021ea70e8ed8/counterexample.json`;
- replay script and log: `checks/audit/021ea70e8ed8/replay.py`, `checks/audit/021ea70e8ed8/replay.log`;
- packaged input payload: `checks/audit/021ea70e8ed8/input.json`;
- supported canonical Racket receipt: `checks/audit/021ea70e8ed8/racket.json`;
- cross-check summary: `checks/audit/021ea70e8ed8/verification.json`.

The optional task-test audit reported **no task-local or selected frozen tests**, exit 5 (`checks/audit/021ea70e8ed8-task-tests/result.json`). No fix was made because this was an audit-only target. A repair should schedule at least one triple-column negative within every three-demo lesson (and similarly reason about mixed columns and horizontal pairs), then declare executable rivals and test all cyclic starts/query rotations.
